    <Axiom id="AX_AUDIT_YAGNI_CROSSCHECK">
      Every symbol `gennady yagni` reports as gated (a Usage Waiver present, per
      `AX_MECHANICAL_VIA_SDD_CHECK`) MUST have both: (1) the `- **Usage Waiver:** <reason>` label
      (or `D-NNN — <reason>` when a genuine Decision Log entry backs it) in its contract/surface
      entry, (2) a `<ts> yagni <name> ← <reason>` line in the round's Execution Log
      (`AX_USAGE_WAIVER_DISCIPLINE`). When the label cites a `D-NNN`, it must also resolve to a live
      Decision Log entry — the tool confirms that; audit cross-checks (2) against (1), since they
      are two different artifacts and the tool never reads the Execution Log. A label with no
      matching log line is `YAGNI_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE` (`MAJOR`): indistinguishable from a
      stale/copy-pasted label never actually decided during this round.
    </Axiom>

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-runtime-backing-verification"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-insight-backflow-capture"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_LANGUAGE_QUALITY_CHECK">
      Operator-facing text of the audited artifacts (spec Vision / Requirements / Decision Log
      bodies, ticket Purpose / Description, README text) must read as a technical document in flat
      engineering Russian — clear to any engineer on the project, junior developer to architect to
      security engineer. Two layers:
      - **Deterministic pre-filter:** `sdd-check` already flags transliterated anglicisms
        (`SDD_LANGUAGE_CALQUE`, warn) — treat every such warning as a finding to route, do not
        re-judge the word list by hand.
      - **Semantic judgment (this audit)** — style AND comprehension, two different failure modes:
        - *Style:* literary or ornate register, English idioms translated word-for-word, sentences a
          busy colleague would stumble on.
        - *Comprehension* (deeper than style — a sentence can be flawless Russian and still be a
          cipher): an **empty label** — an adjective+noun term with no stated opposite («тонкая
          строка» — thin relative to what? is there a «толстая»?) — is unexplained jargon, not a
          description; a **metaphor stated as fact** («у разговора есть дом») instead of the literal
          mechanism («тред хранится как обычная строка ChatEntity») is rare but dangerous, since it
          passes every other filter; a **term whose meaning lives only in code** must be decoded from
          that code and restated in the sentence, never guessed and never left opaque.
        Test both: read it aloud as a mid-level developer (style); then strip the term from your head
        and ask whether you could still act on the sentence (comprehension) — either failure routes.

      → `LANGUAGE_QUALITY` finding with the concrete sentence and a plain-Russian rewrite proposal.
      Canonical tokens (code, IDs, status tokens, BDD keywords, paths) stay English per
      `AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE` and are never flagged.
    </Axiom>

